§9.1/D-10: `@@` is mandatory. A bare head line is **literal text** — it has no
construct touching it, so it is not a decorator and never configures the block
below it (§14):

{.lead, #nope}

> a quote that keeps no extras

The same head with the sigil does decorate the next block, so the two spellings
are not interchangeable:

@@{.lead, #nope}
> a quote that gets both
